Given, $C_p=10$ cals at $1000 \mathrm{~K}$
$$
\begin{aligned}
&T_1=1000 \mathrm{~K} . T_2=100 \mathrm{~K} \\
&m=32 \mathrm{~g}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\Delta S=?
$$
at constant pressure
$$
\begin{aligned}
&\triangle S=C_p \ln \frac{T_2}{T_1} \\
&=2.303 \times C_p \log \frac{T_2}{T_1} \\
&=2.303 \times 10 \log \frac{100}{1000} \\
&=-23.03 \mathrm{cal} \mathrm{deg}^{-1}
\end{aligned}
$$
